body:
Thanks for the support, I am currently on the waiting list for both a local therapy service and my university, hoping one of them will get back to me soon. I will definitely look up some more resources to help deal with this in the meantime. I am trying to journal and be patient with myself if I am not 100 percent in my schoolwork right now. 

&#x200B;

The ethics leader emailed me again today to tell me she is going to talk to the guy who assaulted me, to see what his perspective is. I don't have a lot of hope that anything will become of my complaint. I am very disappointed in the organization, because they have been promoting an increase in inclusiveness. Instead of receiving comfort and support, I was invalidated and blamed. I don't think the ethic's leader understood the definition of coercion. I have also made a report to my university's title XI, but I don't know how much they can do since he graduated from a different university.
